Practical 2.1 – Linear Search (Iterative & Recursive)
2.1 :

a. I learned how the linear search algorithm works in both iterative and recursive approaches to find a target element in a list.

b. At first I was confused about how recursion continues searching without using a loop. It was difficult for me to understand how the index changes after every recursive function call.

c. While implementing both approaches, I realized that the iterative method uses a loop whereas the recursive method uses function calls to achieve the same result. I also observed that since the search stops immediately after finding the target, my program returns the first occurrence of the element if it appears more than once.
